<title>GERMANY: German trade seeks 0.99-6.0 Ecu/T wheat rebate.</title>
<headline>German trade seeks 0.99-6.0 Ecu/T wheat rebate.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders applied for export restitutions in a 0.99-6.0 Ecus a tonne range for 13,500 tonnes of free market soft wheat, intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BLE also received bids to export 1,000 tonnes of free market barley, where it did not disclose the rebate requested.</p>
<p>One trader also bid for the export of 50 tonnes of rice.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
